A||N||6||86SEFIERO||whats the differences between 88 GT and 88 formula||||5||
Z||000000||86SEFIERO||06-07-2000||04:52 AM||||<BR>Im trying to decide what my next fiero will be. What are the main differences between the 88 formulas and 88 GT's? Do both the models have the same raed horsepower v-6's and did all 88's come with the w6 ( im not sure if thats what its called) suspension?||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||06-07-2000||07:31 AM||||88 formula's and GT's had the same engine and suspension combo <B>(which pretty much had nothing to do with lotus)</B>.  <P>the GT's were available with pwr windows, locks, sub woofer, rw defrost, elec trunk, lumbar and leather seats... seems like there was one other difference, cant remember.<P>also, formula's came with black bbs rims, whereas gt's had gold rims that year.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-07-2000||09:28 AM||||The body style was completely different.  The GT was a fastback with the aero body and the Formula was a notchback/coupe with a wing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||PAUL88GT||06-07-2000||01:20 PM||||I have been told that the Formula is slightly faster than the 88GT since it is about 200 lbs lighter.  But, I can't confirm this, since I have not owned a Formula.<P>How many Formulas were made versus the 88GT?  Where is the data base nut when you need him?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||06-07-2000||04:10 PM||||I believe the only options available on the GT, and not the Formula was power mirrors.<P>Faster?  In theory, a lighter car with the same HP engine would be faster.  But a 200 LBS difference wouldn't effect the speed too much.  I've never driven or raced an 88 GT with my Formula, so I cannot confirm it.<P>Production #'s?  I got those too.<P>88 GT      6,848<BR>88 Formula 5,643<BR>88 Coupes 13,910||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula||06-07-2000||06:42 PM||||the formula has the cool decal on the side too!!!!!!!!!<P>most formulas you find will not have pw, or leather or anything like that.  They are mostly stripped.  BUT, thats what makes them so cool.<P>If you want a more luxoriuos sports car then go with the GT and if you want a sports car thats like a roadster (steering, seats, music) style then go with the formula.<P>btw. formula'a are still cheaper than 88 GTs even though they are extremly rare.||||reg||1
Z||000006||sid1200||06-08-2000||04:10 AM||||not sure where everyone gets the Formula's are 200lb lighter deal.<P>the actual weight of a similarly equipped formula to GT is very similar.  maybe 50lbs or so.  I also talked to some forum members who did the GT conversion who did not notice the GT panels weighing any more.<P>most of the weight difference would be from the GT having all the power options which most formulas did not have.  If we are talking about weight, AT's wieght more as well, as do cars with spoilers and sunroofs.  <P>also GT's were avail with both black and gold wheels, the black std, the gold a no cost option||||reg||1
